 "notes": "Chart Eight ledger occupies the right-hand page (117); the left-hand page (116, headed \"HOW TO TRADE IN STOCKS\") carries only the two printed explanatory annotations, no grid. Four rows of carried-forward pivotal figures sit above the \"1939\"/\"DATE\" header row: row 1 (UT columns, black, single black underline: US 71 1/4, BS 77 5/8, KP 148 7/8); row 2 (NRC columns, blue ink with single RED underline: US 61, BS 68 3/4, KP 129 3/4); row 3 (US NR 70 blue no underline; BS/KP UT 80 and 150, black, single black underline); and the \"1939\" row itself (SRC columns, blue, no underline: US 62, BS 69 1/2, KP 131 1/2). All handwritten entries use grid-position + ink-color cross-checks consistent with the stated column-ink convention (UT=black, DT=red, others=blue). Checksums (US+BS=KP) verified for every row with all three instruments except MAR.3, where US 64 7/8 + BS 75 1/4 = 140 1/8 but the written KP is plainly \"140\" (no visible fraction) \u2014 flagged as a discrepancy rather than force-fit. Dates skip Sundays throughout (no Sun rows), and also skip Feb 13 (Mon, observed Lincoln's Birthday since Feb 12 fell on a Sunday) and Feb 22 (Wed, Washington's Birthday) \u2014 both consistent with 1939 NYSE holiday observance, confirming the day-by-day date inference. Page numbers: left page \"116\", right page \"117\".",
